1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,290
Most real parts have only one thickness. You can still do a two-point calibration by using the first and second back-wall echoes from the same step.

2
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:18,590
The second back-wall echo has traveled through the 0.500 inch step twice. To the Epoch, it is a 1.000 inch reflector.

3
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:26,990
The Epoch has been reset. First, set the range so both echoes fit. Press F1 for Basic, then P3 for Range.

4
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:31,270
Press the check key for 1 inch steps, then turn up to 2.000 inches.

5
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:34,580
Place the probe on the 0.500 inch step.

6
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:41,260
Now we see the initial pulse, the first back-wall echo, the second one, and a third further to the right.

7
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:47,150
Press GATES, press check for bigger steps, and move Gate 1 onto the first back-wall echo.

8
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:50,850
Press 2nd F and GATES to bring it to 80 percent.

9
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:57,980
Press F3 for Auto Cal, then P2 for Cal-Zero. Enter 0.500 inch with the knob.

10
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:00,270
Press P6, Continue.

11
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:05,940
Now, do not move the probe. The second point comes from the same spot on the same step.

12
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:10,250
Press GATES and move Gate 1 onto the second back-wall echo.

13
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:15,270
Bring the second echo to 80 percent. It is smaller, so the gain goes up.

14
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:19,380
Press F3 for Auto Cal, then P3 for Cal-Vel.

15
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:27,290
Enter 1.000 inch, not 0.500. The second echo has crossed the step twice. Here the value already reads 1.000.

16
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:29,300
Press P7, Done.

17
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:39,170
Velocity 0.2320 and zero 0.500 microseconds: the same answer as the two-step method, from a single thickness.

18
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:46,690
Check it. Move Gate 1 back to the first back-wall echo, and set it back to 80 percent. It reads 0.500.

19
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:53,010
Now verify on steps you did not use. The 0.200 inch step reads 0.200.

20
00:01:53,010 --> 00:01:57,060
And the 0.400 inch step reads 0.400.

21
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:07,640
Common mistakes: a range too small to show the second echo, moving the probe between Cal-Zero and Cal-Vel, and entering 0.500 for both points.

22
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:11,630
Now try it yourself on the Epoch below.
